Embedded React: treat an explicit scale of 1 as no transform.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json. Changed file: engine/rendering/
transform.c. Proposed upstream as pull request #287.

er_transform_is_translate_only() recognised identity scale only as the unset
value 0. A node whose scale is bound to an animated value resting at 1 (every
focus lift such as whileFocus={{scale: 1.04}} once it settles) therefore stayed
"complex": each repaint captured its whole subtree into the transform scratch
and mapped it back out. Scale 1 with no rotation now takes the plain-offset
path, as 0 does; the damage pre-pass, render pass and hit test share this
predicate, so they stay in agreement.

diff --git a/engine/rendering/transform.c b/engine/rendering/transform.c
--- a/engine/rendering/transform.c
+++ b/engine/rendering/transform.c
@@ -336,7 +336,9 @@
     if (n->tp_rotate_x != 0.0f || n->tp_rotate_y != 0.0f || n->tp_perspective != 0.0f)
         return false;
 #endif
-    return n->tp_scale_x == 0.0f && n->tp_scale_y == 0.0f && n->tp_rotate_z == 0.0f;
+    /* 0 is the unset sentinel; an explicit 1 (a scale animation at rest) is no less an identity. */
+    return (n->tp_scale_x == 0.0f || n->tp_scale_x == 1.0f) && (n->tp_scale_y == 0.0f || n->tp_scale_y == 1.0f)
+           && n->tp_rotate_z == 0.0f;
 }
 
 #if ERUI_3D_TRANSFORMS
